{
 "encounter_id": "00878",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh, I'm terribly sorry I'm late, doctor, I got the wrong day on the calendar, I thought it was Thursday. I mean, it's Thursday, but, oh, never mind. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not at all, Mr Alderton. We have time. How have you been since I last saw you? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Not great, I'm afraid. The stiffness is worse in the mornings, it takes me an hour to get going, and my right hand shakes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "So the stiffness is worse first thing, and the right hand has a tremor. Which hand, again?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The right. Sorry, did I say left? The right."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And how's your walking?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Slow. I shuffle. My wife says I'm like a penguin."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had any falls?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No falls, no. Wobbles, but I've caught myself."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any hallucinations, seeing things that aren't there?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What are you on at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Levodopa, 100 mg, four times a day. The last one's at six, and by seven in the morning I'm worn out."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Right. Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No allergies, none."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And your Parkinson's, remind me when you were diagnosed?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three years ago. Though I think it started a year before."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And you worked as?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I was a bus driver. Retired now."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. Pulse 72, blood pressure 138 over 80, temperature 36.5, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 14, weight 74 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All fine. Hold your arms out in front.",
   "pause": 8.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Like this? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I can see a tremor in the right hand at rest."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, it's a pill-rolling thing. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And when I move your right arm, there's stiffness, a cogwheel catch, but the left is normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that bad? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's what we expect. I think the stiffness in the mornings is the levodopa wearing off between doses."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What can we do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to start rasagiline, 1 mg, once a day, to smooth things out."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will it help the shaking? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A little. I'd also like to arrange a physiotherapy assessment, and blood tests for your kidney and liver function."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If the stiffness isn't better in a month, come back and we'll look at the timing again."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A month. I'll write it down. ~"
  }
 ],
